WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:37.266 --> 00:00:38.566
Hello everyone, I'm Hiker CP.

00:00:38.566 --> 00:00:40.600
Right now, I'm in......

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.333
(a state of confusion)

00:00:42.466 --> 00:00:43.766
doing something I've never done before &gt;///&lt;

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.333
I'm crying.

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.266
I'm really freaking tired!!

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.033
It's so noisy.

00:00:51.233 --> 00:00:52.133
It's so sore.

00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:52.733
It's so hot.

00:00:52.966 --> 00:00:53.900
So much sweat.

00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:55.466
I'm so overwhelmed!

00:00:57.233 --> 00:00:58.433
But I did it!

00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.500
Today,

00:00:59.666 --> 00:01:02.566
let's go back to 24 hours before the event!

00:01:02.866 --> 00:01:03.900
Doggo!

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.166
(Pick up supplies at the event site)

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.666
(You can buy BONT even without shoes!)

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.433
My coach is better than 226! (Easy!)

00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:49.666
Don't cry, don't cry (FXT's crying driver)

00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:03.766
First, set the bike up on top.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.600
The seat can't go on, so I'll just use the handlebars.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.300
Put one bag for the road run.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:15.766
Put the bike in another one.

00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:20.666
Have you ever run a noodle shop? XDD

00:02:22.733 --> 00:02:25.866
Let's start packaging these supplements now.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.000
Two electrolyte tablets of 550 milligrams, and I hope.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.033
Consume over 700 in one hour with black plum pectin.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:33.566
I'll take caffeine roughly every two hours (or 3 hours).

00:02:33.566 --> 00:02:36.233
RC means taking two pills (every 1.5 hours) and then O2.

00:02:36.233 --> 00:02:38.433
Take three pills before going in the water, and the same with taurine.

00:02:38.466 --> 00:02:41.833
Take two pills (every 1.5 hours), so two at a time.

00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:44.766
Distribute three to four pills in these storage boxes.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:50.500
Inside, 226 would suggest adding ten packets.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.600
You can add it to this insulated water bottle.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.566
The gel in the second half will still be cold.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.033
You can fill it with water and freeze it.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.666
Replacement for the aid station.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.600
The COMPRESSPORT one-piece suit is very.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.600
Comfortable. I used to resist wearing one-piece suits.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.233
It was because I thought I couldn't pee, but with this,

00:03:19.266 --> 00:03:22.200
the design allows me to easily relieve myself.

00:03:22.233 --> 00:03:27.133
Let's try spraying this tomorrow.

00:03:27.166 --> 00:03:30.166
What's special is that he combined the socks with OXYGEN.

00:03:30.166 --> 00:03:32.600
He made the leg sleeves on top of that.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.100
This is my first time using this.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.000
I've used socks and leg sleeves before.

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:40.166
I thought about making these long socks directly.

00:03:40.333 --> 00:03:41.766
White socks are the coolest!!

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:42.800
Take a look at this.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.500
Put the running gear here. Hat and gel.

00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:02.866
Capsule and shoes. Remember not to put the socks.

00:04:02.866 --> 00:04:04.500
Put the socks in the bike compartment.

00:04:04.533 --> 00:04:06.933
Loosen the shoelaces a bit.

00:04:06.933 --> 00:04:10.433
Roll up the socks and stuff them in.

00:04:10.433 --> 00:04:13.566
Your shoes have a towel inside.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:20.033
Car, glasses, hat, and race number.

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:24.666
You can wear it directly and tie a knot.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.200
Tie a slip knot to hang it up, then when you take it down,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.366
you can pull it out.

00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:04.000
Get ready to go!

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.466
Swimming is too slow, QQQQQ.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.100
Are we recording a podcast now???

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.633
We have to run really far.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:33.166
Push the cart to the starting line at the gate.

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:50.800
Suddenly going off-road.

00:06:55.233 --> 00:07:02.266
A bit tired, slightly tired.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:06.233
Power is about 190 to 210, pretty intense.

00:07:06.233 --> 00:07:10.066
Pedaling, you can push through the first half lap.

00:07:10.066 --> 00:07:16.966
In just over an hour like this.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.700
Success can be sweet.

00:07:20.766 --> 00:07:21.933
We can only eat the wind.

00:07:22.033 --> 00:07:24.266
Eating wind fills you up. The journey is harder because.

00:07:24.266 --> 00:07:27.433
I feel like there are more uphill climbs. That wind.

00:07:27.433 --> 00:07:30.300
Actually, it's not too bad. I can hold on until the turning point.

00:08:25.566 --> 00:08:31.066
Getting ready to cross the big bridge. Heading to the finish line, T2.

00:08:31.066 --> 00:08:33.966
Okay, I can't go on anymore. My legs don't feel like my legs.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.633
Slower than expected and also more tired.

00:08:36.633 --> 00:08:40.266
More tired than anticipated. I'll just have to see how it goes, I'm exhausted.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:43.900
So tired. Thinking about 113 after 226.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:46.700
Thinking about 515 after 113. After 515, I just want...

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:52.100
I just want to lie at home.

00:08:52.933 --> 00:08:55.433
There are quite a few cars, so.

00:08:55.433 --> 00:08:57.766
We should be ahead, right? It's pretty empty now.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:05.300
We need to walk more. We might cramp up.

00:09:05.333 --> 00:09:07.566
And my sunglasses fell off.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:43.433
The transition took forever, four minutes.

00:09:43.466 --> 00:09:48.700
Okay, this time I'm wearing On running shoes.

00:09:53.433 --> 00:09:55.633
I've only run 300 meters. I'm in trouble, it's too hot.

00:09:55.633 --> 00:09:58.366
Starting with 113 on flat ground. It shouldn't be worse than an IRONMAN.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:03.166
It's pitch black. I'll be running that soon.

00:10:03.166 --> 00:10:05.400
Running to the Living Water Lake, into the forest park.

00:10:05.433 --> 00:10:08.566
It feels a bit like a wildlife zoo. Very similar.

00:10:08.566 --> 00:10:11.733
Like a safari, seeing animals from a jeep.

00:10:11.766 --> 00:10:13.700
Look at the deer
Crocodile ah, peacock ah

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:16.100
I went to Sri Lanka and had fun there.

00:10:16.133 --> 00:10:18.900
This place looks a lot like the Safari I saw.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:20.966
I've never been here before. It's different from Mahengheng.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:24.000
Mahengheng is very lively, but this place isn't.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:28.400
There's just the sun and you, who are about to wither. XD

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:33.233
Okay, I think I can't eat anymore.

00:10:33.233 --> 00:10:35.566
I just ate a third of it.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:38.300
Kiwifruit, Shu run with water
Stomach now

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:40.733
It's bloated. So I decided to just.

00:10:40.766 --> 00:10:42.633
Drink water and use some sponge like this.

00:10:42.666 --> 00:10:45.500
That should be fine. I just stuffed the sponge here.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:46.500
Stuffed a little bit of cream.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.633
It turned into 'sponge cream'.

00:10:48.666 --> 00:10:50.433
My chest muscles cool down better than my forehead!

00:10:50.433 --> 00:10:53.500
The chest muscles are bigger, and the forehead is smaller.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:54.500
Big chest, small forehead?

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.200
Everyone is running really slow. I thought everyone would be like zoom zoom zoom.

00:10:57.366 --> 00:11:00.800
Every four and a half minutes. That's pretty slow.

00:11:00.833 --> 00:11:02.500
At six minutes speed. No wonder they can still be there.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:08.500
Talking. Where are we supposed to run to, I was just thinking.

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:10.033
They said we shouldn't get lost because of the arrows.

00:11:10.066 --> 00:11:17.066
It's all pretty clear. This water is a bit useless.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:20.633
It's just as good as not having it. Still, they put in effort, so thumbs up.

00:11:20.633 --> 00:11:23.133
The living water lake can even run to the living water lake.

00:11:23.166 --> 00:11:25.700
The first lap brings us back to that spot.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.133
I actually don't want to see this lake again.

00:11:28.166 --> 00:11:30.400
It forces you to run, and you run really fast.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:33.500
We quickly reached that little red swimming gate.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:41.533
Keep going! Keep it up!

00:11:55.933 --> 00:11:59.033
Cooling down. It's been three kilometers.

00:11:59.033 --> 00:12:00.066
I've realized something.

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.366
I won't be coming back.

00:12:04.733 --> 00:12:05.266
I'm getting anxious.

00:12:13.333 --> 00:12:14.266
Going uphill.

00:12:27.366 --> 00:12:29.900
(Thanks to the hardworking volunteers!)

00:12:38.666 --> 00:12:41.433
Did you learn the big iced milk tea!?

00:12:41.433 --> 00:12:42.966
10K!

00:12:44.333 --> 00:12:46.200
We're halfway! I'm almost done.

00:12:46.366 --> 00:12:50.166
I'm so tired, I want to go back. I don't know where to go.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:51.766
To a place where there are no people.

00:12:52.366 --> 00:12:53.833
I want to share a CT with everyone.

00:12:53.833 --> 00:12:55.133
It's a story about becoming a Puyuma.

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.133
In a second, it turns into a Puyuma track.

00:12:58.166 --> 00:13:02.600
I don't know how many kilometers to go back.
I don't know, I don't know.

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:03.733
Just run.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:10.400
The 226 players chose this themselves, please move forward XD.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:18.733
Turn around!
Half of the Mahengheng is finally here.

00:13:18.733 --> 00:13:22.300
It's 8K now, if it's 8K,
we still have a long way to run.

00:13:22.333 --> 00:13:26.300
Don't overthink it.
We just need to run, let's take a look.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:28.800
Automatic water supply.
Automatic water supply.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.000
(Eating a pack of FAST sour plum jelly.)

00:13:39.266 --> 00:13:44.133
I'm back.
It's 16, it's 16, it should be 16K.

00:13:44.166 --> 00:13:46.900
I can't do it anymore.
If I can break 6 hours, that's all I ask.

00:13:52.233 --> 00:13:53.766
On the same track as the bicycles.

00:13:56.033 --> 00:14:00.433
I can't do it anymore, I can't figure out the route. I just keep running forward.

00:14:11.033 --> 00:14:15.666
5K. There's nobody.

00:14:18.066 --> 00:14:20.733
I think socks with leg sleeves are really useful. My calves right now.

00:14:20.766 --> 00:14:22.766
I don't feel any cramps. But my thighs are about to cramp.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:25.000
I don't think it's suitable for a triathlon. I should have changed after wearing it too long.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:27.466
You can use leg sleeves with socks.

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:31.800
The clothes are very breathable. They're extremely breathable.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.766
I need to pee. But I think it's almost over.

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:37.800
This one can be sprayed here. Before the race, I.

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:39.900
I've already sprayed twice, so I don't need to during the race.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.966
You can also pee in a one-piece like this. If you want to buy a two-piece.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.033
The problem is that the pants tend to slip down (it's the same idea as choosing suspenders for riding pants).
This jumpsuit doesn't have that issue.

00:14:46.033 --> 00:14:50.266
Its pockets are very useful.
They're really big and can hold a lot.

00:14:50.433 --> 00:14:52.533
They go really deep.
The downside is that they're too expensive.

00:14:52.533 --> 00:14:55.066
You have to be determined to buy them.
If you can't bring yourself to do it,

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:56.966
you won't be able to own them, just like us.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.700
Signing up for 226 keeps getting more expensive every year.

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:01.200
It's inflation, you know.
We still go ahead and buy it anyway, XDD.

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:04.933
We rush in and fight for it, no matter how tough it gets.

00:15:04.933 --> 00:15:06.833
There will be chatting going on here.

00:15:06.866 --> 00:15:08.866
Track photographers.

00:15:08.866 --> 00:15:11.400
Slacking off in such a cool place.

00:15:11.433 --> 00:15:15.533
Do you have to pay extra for photos??
Why is the uphill bridge so tiring?

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:27.433
I see the sea! 
Go into the main road for 1K!

00:15:28.766 --> 00:15:31.933
This used to be the entrance for everyone, but now

00:15:31.933 --> 00:15:34.333
it's been moved to the stadium.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:37.233
My legs don't feel like my legs anymore.

00:15:45.933 --> 00:15:47.500
Trail running.

00:15:47.933 --> 00:15:49.433
The game I've never played is about to end!!!

00:15:50.133 --> 00:15:55.700
I've come in. 
This game is really about to end.

00:15:55.733 --> 00:15:59.533
It's over. 
It's really over.

00:16:02.566 --> 00:16:05.733
Entering the playground.

00:16:05.833 --> 00:16:07.200
I have to run half around the field.

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:13.400
I'm so tired, and there are so many people saying hi.

00:16:13.566 --> 00:16:16.633
This atmosphere is quite nice.

00:16:16.633 --> 00:16:21.833
You can have it if you pay!! 
It's really easy to get.

00:16:21.866 --> 00:16:27.633
Got it. 
I'm so tired, I can't take it anymore.

00:16:27.633 --> 00:16:32.233
I'm exhausted, I can't take it anymore.

00:16:35.266 --> 00:16:39.133
I almost went the wrong way (almost walked into the arch at 226).
We're heading now.

00:16:39.133 --> 00:16:42.933
We need to go to the finish line, but we have to take a longer route this time.

00:16:42.933 --> 00:16:45.100
We're 300 meters over time!!

00:16:45.333 --> 00:16:47.933
It's 21.2K.
We're over time, but more is included at no extra charge.

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:54.366
We're about to finish.
The finish line.

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.166
We did it.

00:17:09.133 --> 00:17:12.733
Thank you, thank you.

00:17:14.233 --> 00:17:18.933
Is this for real? We finished.

00:17:18.933 --> 00:17:21.733
It's over.
Finished.

00:17:25.466 --> 00:17:32.033
Anyway, I'm back.
This time, this time.

00:17:32.133 --> 00:17:33.133
That was so useless, XDD.

00:17:33.133 --> 00:17:35.566
Overall, I think my performance was.

00:17:36.233 --> 00:17:39.400
I'm 'satisfied but not satisfied.'
Not satisfied at all.

00:17:39.433 --> 00:17:42.233
I reached my expected time
because I got injured.

00:17:42.233 --> 00:17:44.466
I didn't train much afterward
so I'm satisfied.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:47.900
I finished without injuries or cramps.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.800
This was my first time participating in a race like this.

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:52.166
CHALLENGE TAIWAN
is really suitable for fun.

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:54.433
It's a fun competition
but the experience was tough.

00:17:54.433 --> 00:17:56.666
It wasn't very enjoyable.
I had only competed in.

00:17:56.666 --> 00:18:00.400
226 and 515.
I competed in 113.

00:18:00.433 --> 00:18:01.700
IRONMAN.
But Ironman has elevation.

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:03.833
So this was my first time in a formal.

00:18:03.866 --> 00:18:06.166
113 competition.
I completed it.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:09.566
I feel my swimming is very weak.
I really struggled.

00:18:09.566 --> 00:18:12.100
I was all over the place, like a snake.

00:18:12.133 --> 00:18:13.966
The bike ride took about 15 minutes longer.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.133
The time difference was expected, but...

00:18:16.133 --> 00:18:17.933
The one-way trip didn't go as I expected.

00:18:17.933 --> 00:18:20.200
I still have about ten minutes to reach my goal.

00:18:20.233 --> 00:18:22.666
Given the distance, I think I'm doing pretty well.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.733
I can still keep running; I won't need to stop.

00:18:25.733 --> 00:18:28.000
Walking like this won't even last five minutes.

00:18:28.033 --> 00:18:29.600
I originally thought if I felt good, I would...

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:32.233
Set a five-minute pace, and then we'll take a break.

00:18:32.266 --> 00:18:36.100
Let's rest a bit, because after today, there's still a very...

00:18:36.133 --> 00:18:38.633
important task; my competition isn't over yet.

00:18:38.633 --> 00:18:41.866
I need to go be a supporter for my competition.

00:18:41.866 --> 00:18:45.900
Wait for A Fei to come back. Because he is the first 226.

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:49.300
I believe the full marathon of the first 226 is the scariest thing.

00:18:49.333 --> 00:18:51.600
Before the race, I didn't tell him what to do.

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:55.066
What are you doing? Let's just watch it later. Dog!

00:19:01.166 --> 00:19:04.900
Come on, take it slow. I'll wait for you when I go out. (T2 180K just came back)

00:19:04.900 --> 00:19:07.366
Currently, the women's total is 10!! That's a lie. Really.

00:19:15.066 --> 00:19:17.166
Now we need to make a plan.

00:19:17.166 --> 00:19:21.666
What does it add up to? 155.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:22.966
I want to give you a surprise. I want to give you a surprise.

00:19:22.966 --> 00:19:25.700
Did you know? The ground is full of UP pectin. Haha.

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:28.533
I only ran once, and I'm about to break down.

00:19:28.566 --> 00:19:31.000
It's like an octopus running twice for me.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.666
The plan is to run at seven and a half minutes.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:36.333
I have a surprise for you. (What surprise?) I want to run with you.

00:19:36.333 --> 00:19:37.266
Together, we will run a full marathon.

00:19:37.266 --> 00:19:38.033
You're kidding.

00:19:38.033 --> 00:19:38.733
No, I'm serious.

00:19:39.733 --> 00:19:41.266
How can this be so good?

00:19:41.366 --> 00:19:44.066
I'll tell you during the race. I'm so happy, how about you?

00:19:44.066 --> 00:19:47.533
My stomach hurts from laughing. XDDD (I talked too much.)

00:19:47.566 --> 00:19:49.500
We have to run this octopus route three times.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:53.000
Oh no, I don't want to know. (Feeling existential.) Three times, really?

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:56.100
You look so pitiful. Take a picture of yourself.

00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:58.633
Poor people, poor dogs. I have to run three laps.

00:19:58.666 --> 00:20:00.600
Today, I'm the only one running three laps.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:02.866
Give me one more medal
Give me more.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:03.766
A towel.

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:07.266
Total 10ing.

00:20:09.833 --> 00:20:10.966
Just keep talking, 42K is fine.

00:20:10.966 --> 00:20:14.400
Then it will go smoothly.
Time chatting will pass quickly.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:20.933
Ah, today I will become an ultra marathon runner.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:22.933
I won't participate in triathlons anymore.

00:20:35.166 --> 00:20:39.100
As long as our feet don't stop,
we will reach the finish line.

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:52.400
Eat a chicken butt
(I will definitely regret it).

00:20:54.133 --> 00:20:56.700
Maha Heng Heng in outer space.

00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:58.866
Come back
Maha Heng Heng from outer space.

00:20:58.866 --> 00:21:01.700
In the human world,
Maha Heng Heng in CT is like outer space.

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:03.133
There are many people on the Puyuma.

00:21:03.133 --> 00:21:06.433
CT is where humans are.

00:21:06.466 --> 00:21:08.100
Everyone is an alien.

00:21:08.133 --> 00:21:09.100
This is how aliens are.

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:10.266
I'm back.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:19.866
(Can you run with me every time?)
There won't be a next time for 226 XDD.

00:21:21.566 --> 00:21:23.933
(I can't do it anymore.)

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:32.100
Back to the zoo.
Now running the third lap.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:35.733
My legs are tight.
But I can still move.

00:21:35.733 --> 00:21:37.300
She's about to give up, her expression is getting worse.

00:21:48.033 --> 00:21:49.100
Just get in the car.

00:21:54.133 --> 00:21:55.233
There's a strange noise.

00:21:57.166 --> 00:22:00.700
You need to save me.
It's so tempting (want to get in the car).

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:05.866
25K, we'll return to the center soon.

00:22:05.866 --> 00:22:08.733
It's 28K.
We're heading back to the finish.

00:22:08.733 --> 00:22:11.166
We're almost there.
She's not doing well, usually past 226.

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:14.300
After the half marathon, it gets really tough mentally.

00:22:14.333 --> 00:22:17.300
A reaction to DOWN
That's how 226 is.

00:22:17.300 --> 00:22:19.200
If things are good up front
It doesn't necessarily mean it's good.

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:22.133
Half a marathon being good is good
If it's not good, then it's just not good.

00:22:22.133 --> 00:22:23.400
Talking nonsense.

00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:29.000
Just keep her company.

00:22:29.033 --> 00:22:31.500
Just be with her.
No need to say much, just run with her.

00:22:31.533 --> 00:22:34.800
Being a straight guy
Is just this simple.

00:22:35.100 --> 00:22:36.233
Next time your partner runs 226,

00:22:36.400 --> 00:22:39.366
Just run the full marathon with them.
That'll be fine.

00:22:39.966 --> 00:22:41.933
Passing is 80 points.
So tired.

00:22:47.333 --> 00:22:48.366
28K.

00:22:49.666 --> 00:22:52.533
3 hours 45.

00:22:56.433 --> 00:23:00.633
You're great.
28, the last stretch.

00:23:05.866 --> 00:23:09.466
Can't even pinch it anymore, lost weight.

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:11.566
Change body fat to 10%.

00:23:14.800 --> 00:23:16.366
The last round, Mahengheng.

00:23:23.833 --> 00:23:24.933
Turn back.

00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:33.933
We're back at the wildlife park, and there are people.

00:23:54.333 --> 00:23:56.333
Not yet, don't worry, don't worry, you don't want to hurry

00:24:10.666 --> 00:24:12.400
Finally, sprint on the field at a pace of three and a half minutes!

00:24:26.366 --> 00:24:29.400
13 hours, 59 minutes, 53 seconds!

00:24:29.400 --> 00:24:31.766
SUB14! Yay!

00:24:43.800 --> 00:24:47.900
(I feel a bit tipsy after running XDDDD)

00:24:49.366 --> 00:24:52.000
I don't know how to end this 155K.

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:54.100
Have you ever done this? If you want to join,

00:24:54.100 --> 00:24:55.800
It's a very joyful atmosphere.

00:24:55.800 --> 00:24:58.300
You can come to CT. I also suggest training should be 'gradual'.

00:24:58.533 --> 00:25:00.000
It's about one to two months after an injury.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.700
I haven't trained.
So even though I feel okay,

00:25:02.700 --> 00:25:04.866
I'm not uncomfortable or anything,
but it's still quite painful.

00:25:05.033 --> 00:25:06.833
If in the future you all have a partner,

00:25:06.833 --> 00:25:10.033
and want to participate in an Ironman event,

00:25:10.033 --> 00:25:13.266
hurry up and train for a full marathon, guys.
(I advise you to quickly train; it's more practical.)

00:25:13.266 --> 00:25:15.400
You need to train for a full marathon to handle it.

00:25:15.400 --> 00:25:19.033
If your partner is into Ironman events,

00:25:19.066 --> 00:25:21.366
today, after finishing, I rested for about an hour,

00:25:21.400 --> 00:25:22.900
then hurried back just in time.

00:25:22.900 --> 00:25:25.500
It really feels like fate.
As soon as I left, I started running,

00:25:25.500 --> 00:25:28.166
and I've been running ever since.
I'm really, really exhausted.

00:25:28.200 --> 00:25:31.700
My legs aren't my legs anymore. It is what it is.

00:25:31.700 --> 00:25:35.133
That's it for today's CT flat road 113 video.

00:25:35.133 --> 00:25:36.000
If you like my videos, feel free to join.

00:25:38.266 --> 00:25:39.033
I'm Hiker CP

00:25:39.066 --> 00:25:40.333
See you next time on the mountain.

00:25:40.333 --> 00:25:41.666
Bye.

00:25:51.800 --> 00:25:56.966
I have become IRONLEG!

